# Every artifact in this subtree is written by `v3_predict.write_sidecar`,
# which pins UTF-8 and LF so that "a sidecar whose bytes depend on the
# platform cannot be checksummed" holds. Three of them are addressed by a
# SHA-256 in a checksum file beside them — `cases.json`, `ig_subset.json` and
# `v3_noise_floor.json` — and `core.autocrlf` is true in this repo, so without
# this line a fresh Windows checkout would materialise CRLF and every one of
# those digests would stop matching the bytes on disk. `v3_report` verifies
# the floor's and the case table's digests when it reads them back, so the
# reports would refuse to build rather than quietly disagree.
*.json text eol=lf
